    "Checking the published package.": "Checking the outgiven bundle.",
    "A newer Android package is on the website. Download it, then install it. Export from Data first if you want a copy.": "A newer Android bundle is on the webstead. Download it, then set it in. Send out from Givens first if you want a likeness.",
    "This package matches the one on the website.": "This bundle matches the one on the webstead.",
    "The website package could not be read. Nothing was downloaded.": "The webstead bundle could not be read. Nothing was downloaded.",
    "When this is on, a check can see the Android package published with the website. Nothing downloads until you ask.": "When this is on, a look over can see the Android bundle outgiven with the webstead. Nothing downloads until you ask.",
    "A life, with the ordinary notes outnumbering the quotations. It can be removed.": "A life, with the everyday writs outnumbering the saws. It can be taken off.",
    "Notes is everything kept. Media counts pictures and clips saved in the journal, not an address that still points elsewhere. Size is the whole backup. In media is how much of that backup those files take. Allowance is what this browser will give the site. Used is everything the site has stored. Remaining is the rest.": "Writs is everything kept. Sights counts bilds and clips kept in the daybook, not a path that still aims elsewhere. Bulk is the whole backup. In sights is how much of that backup those packs take. Headroom is what this weblooker will give the stead. Used is everything the stead has hoarded. Leftover is the rest.",
    "The browser is a tab. The installed site is the home screen copy. Each can keep pictures, including link previews, or not. They share one store. If that space fills, a new note may not be saved.": "The weblooker is a tab. The inset stead is the home screen build. Each can keep bilds, along with link forelooks, or not. They share one hoard. If that room fills, a new writ may not be kept.",
    "Choose a file this app can keep open, including one in a folder that already syncs, such as Syncthing. The permission stays, so the file is read and written on its own. The newer note is kept. A deletion travels too. The layout stays on this device. A sealed journal is not written there. Unseal on both devices, then seal again after.": "Choose a pack this tool can keep open, along with one in a holder that already yokes, such as Syncthing. The leave stays, so the pack is read and written on its own. The newer writ is kept. A wipe travels too. The outlay stays on this gear. A clasped daybook is not written there. Unclasp on both gears, then clasp again after.",
    "The words, the language, and a source if you have one.": "The words, the tongue, and a wellspring if you have one.",
